# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# Generated project output workspace (disposable, per CLAUDE.md)
generated/*
!generated/.gitkeep

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Orchestrator runtime state (local kitaru store + run logs)
orchestrator/.kitaru/
orchestrator/runlog/

# Playwright artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Secrets — never committed
.env
*.env
# The Docker env file (compose.yaml's `env_file`). It holds WEBGEN_MASTER_KEY,
# the AES-256-GCM key every stored API key is encrypted under. Needs its own
# line: `.env` matches only that exact name and `*.env` matches only names
# ENDING in `.env`, so `.env.docker` slipped past both and `git status` offered
# it for commit. `/.env.*` covers any future sibling (.env.local, …) too.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and that matters: an unanchored `.env.*` matches
# at every level, which would cover `editor/.env.hosted` — a file that is
# committed on purpose (it is what makes `npm run dev:hosted` hosted mode, and it
# holds no secret). Being already tracked, it would not actually have been
# dropped, but the rule would be lying about intent.
/.env.*

# Identity database (argon2 hashes, live session ids, and — from slice 3 —
# encrypted API keys). Ignore the directory, not just the filename: WAL mode
# also writes -wal and -shm siblings alongside identity.db, and those hold
# recent committed data too.
server/data/
# ...and the same database anywhere else. `node server/scripts/user.ts` resolves
# --db RELATIVE TO CWD and defaults to ./data/identity.db, so running it from
# the repo root creates a repo-root data/ holding exactly the same secrets.
# Found by following the README literally (task 6): `git status` offered
# `?? data/` for commit. The dropped-value guard in user.ts now makes the
# common cause fail loudly; this covers the rest.
data/

# Misc
coverage/
*.local
.DS_Store